new = '''//! The main formatting loop.
//!
//! Formatting proceeds line by line. The source text is first cleaned
//! up by collapsing runs of blank lines, replacing tabs when indenting
//! with spaces, and removing trailing spaces. The resulting lines are
//! then placed on a queue, together with their original line numbers,
//! and processed in order.
//!
//! For each line taken from the queue:
//!
//! 1. The ignore state is updated according to any `% tex-fmt: skip`,
//!    `% tex-fmt: off` or `% tex-fmt: on` directives, and the verbatim
//!    state is updated according to any verbatim environments which
//!    begin or end on the line. Lines which are ignored or verbatim
//!    are passed through to the output unchanged.
//!
//! 2. If the line contains an environment or item command after some
//!    other text, the line is split at that point. The first part
//!    continues to be processed as the current line, while the
//!    remainder is placed back on the queue to be processed next.
//!
//! 3. The indentation of the line is calculated from the indentation
//!    state left by the previous line, and applied to the line.
//!
//! 4. If the indented line is longer than the wrap length, an attempt
//!    is made to wrap it. If successful, both parts are placed back on
//!    the queue, and the state computed for the line is discarded so
//!    that the parts are processed afresh.
//!
//! 5. Otherwise the line is added to the output and the new state is
//!    committed.
//!
//! Finally the output lines are joined, trailing spaces are removed,
//! and warnings are recorded if the indentation did not return to zero
//! or ever became negative.
'''
assert old in src
src = src.replace(old, new, 1)
open('/workspace/src/format.rs','w').write(src)
